  "chief_complaint": "Frequent emergency visits driven by cardiovascular, renal and neurocognitive complications in a frail 96\u2011year\u2011old with multimorbidity",
  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient has a lifelong history of obesity, hypertension, hyperlipidemia and type 2 diabetes diagnosed in the 1950s. Over decades this metabolic syndrome progressed to ischemic heart disease requiring coronary artery bypass grafting in 1972, diabetic microvascular complications (retinopathy, neuropathy, proteinuria, microalbuminuria) and chronic kidney disease now at stage 4. Alzheimer\u2019s disease was diagnosed in 1996, leading to severe cognitive decline. Anemia, hypertriglyceridemia and chronic oral disease are present. Social isolation and limited social contact have been documented since 2014, and a record of full\u2011time employment at age 96 is likely erroneous. Recent vital signs show normal blood pressure and heart rate, and hemoglobin A1c is within target, but renal function and lipid panels are missing. The pattern of 172 emergency visits versus only 2 outpatient visits indicates a reactive care model with high acute\u2011care utilization.",
